---
to: "docs/domain-capability/domain-capability-contract.md"
sparql:
  rows: |
    PREFIX dcp: <https://ggen.dev/ontology/domain-capability#>
    PREFIX dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>
    PREFIX qce: <https://ggen.dev/ontology/qualified-capability-ecology#>
    SELECT ?identifier ?authority ?providerPackage ?providerModule ?version ?available ?ceiling WHERE {
      ?cap a dcp:DomainCapability ; dcterms:identifier ?identifier ; dcp:authorityRequirement ?authority .
      ?realization a dcp:Realization ; dcp:realizes ?cap ;
          dcp:providerPackage ?providerPackage ; dcp:providerModule ?providerModule .
      OPTIONAL { ?realization dcp:providerVersion ?version }
      OPTIONAL { ?realization dcp:available ?available }
      OPTIONAL { ?realization qce:authorityEnvelope ?env . ?env qce:authorityCeiling ?ceiling }
    } ORDER BY ?identifier ?providerModule
---
# Domain capability contract (projection -- a consequence, never the source)

Every row below echoes literals already stored in this pack's admitted ontology
(`dcp:DomainCapability` x `dcp:Realization` bindings). Nothing is synthesized;
projections are re-admitted nowhere.

Capability IDs are the pinned dotted identifiers (`dcterms:identifier`), joined by
the consumer's resolver (`ash_pplan v26.9.30`). `ceiling` is the realization's bound
`qce:authorityCeiling`; availability without a ceiling that admits the capability's
authority requirement is refused by `gates/070_availability_requires_authority.rq`.

